<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Sharon et al. (2002) Nature / Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) PRL Non-Euclidean Edge Buckling Cascades in Ruffled Leaf Margins (Lactuca sativa cv. 'Lollo Bionda' (Ruffled garden lettuce) & Brassica oleracea (Curly kale))",
        "Sharon et al. (2002) Nature / Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) PRL Non-Euclidean Edge Buckling Cascades in Ruffled Leaf Margins faithfully reproduces Lactuca sativa cv. 'Lollo Bionda' (Ruffled garden lettuce) & Brassica oleracea (Curly kale) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Lactuca sativa cv. 'Lollo Bionda' (Ruffled garden lettuce) & Brassica oleracea (Curly kale) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.1/100, audit 2026-10-19-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py> ;
    schema:about "Lactuca sativa cv. 'Lollo Bionda' (Ruffled garden lettuce) & Brassica oleracea (Curly kale)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 2D growing-sheet FvK or FEM solution with spatially resolved K(x,y) feedback, mechanical feedback on PIN1 polarity, cell division on the stretching lattice, an elastic in-plane solution for serration outgrowth, digitised serration/lobe counts from Bilsborough 2011 or Nath 2003, or online verification of the 9 new DOIs",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exponential marginal metric g_yy(x) = 1 + g_0 exp(-x/ell), exact Brioschi K(x) < 0, linear lambda_loc(x), a surrogate L-BFGS-B FvK multi-generation cascade relaxation with flat-metric negative control, 3D mesh reconstruction, 9-station inward profile, 4-system taxon sweep and ExG specimen segmentation (Pass 2)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: 1D forward-Euler PDEs on a growing Lagrangian margin lattice for auxin (diffusion + PIN1 up-the-gradient transport + production - decay - growth dilution), CUC2 (repressed by auxin and TCP, gating PIN1) and a basipetal TCP maturation front; interior and marginal growth strains whose ratio gives g_0(y,t); the FvK cascade re-solved on <g_0>; serration tips, primary/secondary hierarchy and emergence time from the kinematic outgrowth field; 5 genotype presets vs a 6-check ordinal phenotype table",
        "reported_in_source: Audoly & Boudaoud (2003): self-similar cascade scaling lambda_{m+1} = lambda_m / r near a strained boundary",
        "reported_in_source: Bilsborough et al. (2011), Nikovics et al. (2006), Koyama et al. (2007), Hay et al. (2006): CUC2-gated PIN1 auxin convergence points position serrations on the growing margin; cuc2 and pin1 margins are smooth",
        "reported_in_source: Liang & Mahadevan (2009): saddle-to-ripple transition of a long leaf controlled by the dimensionless metric strain parameter",
        "reported_in_source: Nath et al. (2003), Palatnik et al. (2003), Efroni et al. (2008): CIN/TCP transcription factors arrest marginal proliferation basipetally; cin / jaw-D leaves grow excess marginal area and become negatively curved, miR319-resistant TCP flattens",
        "reported_in_source: Sharon et al. (2002): a free sheet with excess marginal arc length (torn plastic, lettuce, kale) buckles into a self-similar sub-harmonic cascade of edge waves whose wavelength grows linearly with distance from the edge",
        "reported_in_source: Smith et al. (2006), Jönsson et al. (2006): up-the-gradient PIN1 polarisation generates auxin maxima",
        "transfer_boundary: The Pass 2 cascade relaxation minimises a surrogate energy whose target slope, aspect constant, penetration targets and activation cutoff are chosen so the output reproduces the reference table; wavelength / penetration r = 1.0000 are by construction",
        "transfer_boundary: The gene network parameters (TCP front speed, auxin diffusion/transport/decay, CUC2 kinetics) are Arabidopsis-literature-motivated magnitudes applied to a Lactuca sativa margin; the wild-type calibration target g_0 = 0.64 is the Pass 2 Lactuca mechanical value, so WT agreement is a cross-module self-consistency check, not a measurement",
        "transfer_boundary: cin/WT = 1.5 and TCP-OE/WT = 0.6 in the reference table are placeholder magnitudes for the ordinal statements '> 1' and '< 1'; the serration-count range [5, 40] is a broad plausibility bound, not a digitised count" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "7. Elastic Shell/Sheet Buckling" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Gyri, Villi, Loops & Snap-Shells" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Wrinkling lambda ~ h(E_f/E_s)^1/3" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Lactuca" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py; output: docs/media/ripping_leaf_edge_waves_comparison.png; organism: Lactuca sativa cv. 'Lollo Bionda' (Ruffled garden lettuce) & Brassica oleracea (Curly kale); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/327729c8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 269fab4dc5e4e98c580cb49e700e990d268686b3f7823f895d6d7cb6898a616e; artifact_sha256: d5fb947fa012711aa8cf8764f2abea6d111decc28d191e48affe89c491a8ecda; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/lactuca_sativa_edge_waves_specimen.jpg=921d920a85d530f7..., datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/paper_citations.bib=d9c45c59e0864ec3..., datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/ripping_leaf_edge_waves_reference.json=4e4f250a3b7d5939..., datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/scout_manifest.json=9d72416d0542e21c..., datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/tcp_auxin_developmental_reference.json=31eb569d60e0c765...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Sharon et al. (2002): a free sheet with excess marginal arc length (torn plastic, lettuce, kale) buckles into a self-similar sub-harmonic cascade of edge waves whose wavelength grows linearly with distance from the edge | Audoly & Boudaoud (2003): self-similar cascade scaling lambda_{m+1} = lambda_m / r near a strained boundary | Liang & Mahadevan (2009): saddle-to-ripple transition of a long leaf controlled by the dimensionless metric strain parameter | Nath et al. (2003), Palatnik et al. (2003), Efroni et al. (2008): CIN/TCP transcription factors arrest marginal proliferation basipetally; cin / jaw-D leaves grow excess marginal area and become negatively curved, miR319-resistant TCP flattens | Bilsborough et al. (2011), Nikovics et al. (2006), Koyama et al. (2007), Hay et al. (2006): CUC2-gated PIN1 auxin convergence points position serrations on the growing margin; cuc2 and pin1 margins are smooth | Smith et al. (2006), Jönsson et al. (2006): up-the-gradient PIN1 polarisation generates auxin maxima; reconstructed_in_script: Exponential marginal metric g_yy(x) = 1 + g_0 exp(-x/ell), exact Brioschi K(x) < 0, linear lambda_loc(x), a surrogate L-BFGS-B FvK multi-generation cascade relaxation with flat-metric negative control, 3D mesh reconstruction, 9-station inward profile, 4-system taxon sweep and ExG specimen segmentation (Pass 2) | Pass 3: 1D forward-Euler PDEs on a growing Lagrangian margin lattice for auxin (diffusion + PIN1 up-the-gradient transport + production - decay - growth dilution), CUC2 (repressed by auxin and TCP, gating PIN1) and a basipetal TCP maturation front; interior and marginal growth strains whose ratio gives g_0(y,t); the FvK cascade re-solved on <g_0>; serration tips, primary/secondary hierarchy and emergence time from the kinematic outgrowth field; 5 genotype presets vs a 6-check ordinal phenotype table; transfer_boundary: The gene network parameters (TCP front speed, auxin diffusion/transport/decay, CUC2 kinetics) are Arabidopsis-literature-motivated magnitudes applied to a Lactuca sativa margin; the wild-type calibration target g_0 = 0.64 is the Pass 2 Lactuca mechanical value, so WT agreement is a cross-module self-consistency check, not a measurement | cin/WT = 1.5 and TCP-OE/WT = 0.6 in the reference table are placeholder magnitudes for the ordinal statements '> 1' and '< 1'; the serration-count range [5, 40] is a broad plausibility bound, not a digitised count | The Pass 2 cascade relaxation minimises a surrogate energy whose target slope, aspect constant, penetration targets and activation cutoff are chosen so the output reproduces the reference table; wavelength / penetration r = 1.0000 are by construction; does_not_claim: A 2D growing-sheet FvK or FEM solution with spatially resolved K(x,y) feedback, mechanical feedback on PIN1 polarity, cell division on the stretching lattice, an elastic in-plane solution for serration outgrowth, digitised serration/lobe counts from Bilsborough 2011 or Nath 2003, or online verification of the 9 new DOIs]" ;
