<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Isometric Marginal Arc-Length Excess Accommodation & Flat-Sheet Stability Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that out-of-plane sinusoidal edge buckling preserves isometric arc length along the stretched margin with aspect ratio A/λ = √(g_yy - 1)/(√2 π), while vanishing identically (A = 0) for a flat Euclidean metric (g_yy = 1) | Variables: g_yy(x): longitudinal target metric component along the leaf margin; A_m(x): out-of-plane wave amplitude of generation m (mm); λ_m: wave wavelength of generation m (mm); g_0: edge excess arc-length strain factor" ;
    dct:source "Sharon, Roman, Marder, Shin & Swinney (2002) Nature 419(6907):579-580; Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) Phys. Rev. Lett. 91(8):086105" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L151-L367>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_067_ripping_leaf_edge_waves.lean#L31-L51> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def isometric_excess_amplitude_rhs (g_excess lam : Int) : Int :=
  g_excess * (lam * lam)
theorem sharon_isometric_arclength_accommodation (g_excess lam : Int) :
    isometric_excess_amplitude_rhs 0 lam = 0 ∧
    isometric_excess_amplitude_rhs g_excess 0 = 0 ∧
    isometric_excess_amplitude_rhs g_excess (-lam) = isometric_excess_amplitude_rhs g_excess lam ∧
    (∀ g l : Nat, 0 < isometric_excess_amplitude_rhs ((g : Int) + 1) ((l : Int) + 1))
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "1 + (1/4) Σ_m (2π A_m(x) / λ_m)^2 = g_yy(x) = 1 + g_0 exp(-x/ℓ)  ⇒  A_m / λ_m ∝ √(g_yy - 1),  g_0 = 0 ⇒ A_m = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/419579a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature01958>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng1835>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0911954106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1015162108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.91.086105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.044792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.045617>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.107.057521>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1079354>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1511/2004.3.254> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Non-Euclidean Föppl–von Kármán Thin-Sheet Elasticity, Negative Gaussian Curvature (K < 0) & Self-Similar Multi-Generation Edge Buckling Cascades" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.isometric_excess_amplitude_rhs" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.sharon_isometric_arclength_accommodation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Negative Intrinsic Gaussian Curvature of Convexly Decaying Marginal Growth Metric" ;
    dct:description "Establishes by Gauss's Theorema Egregium that any convexly decaying marginal growth profile (g''_yy(x) > 0) induces strictly negative Gaussian curvature K(x) < 0 near the free edge, forcing out-of-plane hyperbolic buckling | Variables: K(x): intrinsic Gaussian curvature of the leaf margin metric (mm^-2); g''_yy(x): second transverse derivative of target metric; ℓ: boundary decay length (mm)" ;
    dct:source "Sharon et al. (2002) Nature 419:579-580; Liang & Mahadevan (2009) PNAS 106(52):22049-22054" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L151-L195>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_067_ripping_leaf_edge_waves.lean#L65-L78> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def marginal_metric_gaussian_curvature_lead (g_yy_xx : Int) : Int :=
  -g_yy_xx
theorem sharon_negative_gaussian_curvature (g_yy_xx : Int) :
    marginal_metric_gaussian_curvature_lead 0 = 0 ∧
    (∀ c : Nat, marginal_metric_gaussian_curvature_lead ((c : Int) + 1) < 0) ∧
    marginal_metric_gaussian_curvature_lead (-g_yy_xx) = g_yy_xx
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "ds^2 = dx^2 + g_yy(x) dy^2,  K(x) = -(1 / √g_yy) d^2(√g_yy)/dx^2 ≈ -(1/2) g''_yy(x) = -(g_0 / 2ℓ^2) exp(-x/ℓ) < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/419579a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature01958>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng1835>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0911954106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1015162108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.91.086105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.044792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.045617>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.107.057521>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1079354>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1511/2004.3.254> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Non-Euclidean Föppl–von Kármán Thin-Sheet Elasticity, Negative Gaussian Curvature (K < 0) & Self-Similar Multi-Generation Edge Buckling Cascades" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.marginal_metric_gaussian_curvature_lead" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.sharon_negative_gaussian_curvature" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Self-Similar Multi-Generation Sub-Harmonic Wavelength Cascade & Linear Boundary Scaling Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves multiplicative self-similar wavelength coarsening across buckling generations and linear growth of dominant wavelength with inward distance x from the leaf margin above the thickness cutoff λ_min ∝ t | Variables: r_cascade: sub-harmonic period-multiplying cascade ratio; λ_m: generation-m wavelength (mm); x: inward distance from the free leaf margin (mm); λ_min(t): finite-thickness cutoff wavelength (mm)" ;
    dct:source "Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) Phys. Rev. Lett. 91(8):086105; Sharon et al. (2002) Nature 419:579-580" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L197-L514>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_067_ripping_leaf_edge_waves.lean#L92-L120> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cascade_next_wavelength (r_cascade lam_m : Int) : Int :=
  r_cascade * lam_m
def local_edge_wavelength (c_lam x lam_min : Int) : Int :=
  c_lam * x + lam_min
theorem audoly_self_similar_cascade_scaling (r_cascade lam_m c_lam lam_min : Int) :
    local_edge_wavelength c_lam 0 lam_min = lam_min ∧
    cascade_next_wavelength r_cascade (cascade_next_wavelength r_cascade lam_m) =
      (r_cascade * r_cascade) * lam_m ∧
    (∀ r l : Nat, ((l : Int) + 1) < cascade_next_wavelength ((r : Int) + 2) ((l : Int) + 1))
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "λ_m / λ_{m+1} = r_cascade ∈ [3, 5],  x_m ∝ λ_m,  λ_loc(x) = c_λ x + λ_min(t)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/419579a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature01958>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng1835>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0911954106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1015162108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.91.086105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.044792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.045617>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.107.057521>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1079354>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1511/2004.3.254> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Non-Euclidean Föppl–von Kármán Thin-Sheet Elasticity, Negative Gaussian Curvature (K < 0) & Self-Similar Multi-Generation Edge Buckling Cascades" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.cascade_next_wavelength" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.audoly_self_similar_cascade_scaling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "CIN/TCP-Arrested, Auxin-Boosted Marginal Growth Increment & Non-Negative Developmental Excess Metric (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that TCP maturation arrests marginal growth, that a slower cin arrest front never yields less growth (excess marginal growth and K < 0 in cin), that the auxin boost keeps margin growth ≥ interior growth so the developmental excess metric g_0 is non-negative and reduces exactly to the flat Euclidean control when β a = 0 | Variables: m(y,t): CIN/TCP maturation (growth-arrest) field in [0,1] sweeping basipetally at speed v_tcp (mm/h); Γ_int, Γ_mar: interior and marginal growth strains; a: auxin level (a.u.); β: auxin growth boost; g_0(y,t): excess metric handed to the Föppl-von Kármán solver" ;
    dct:source "Nath, Crawford, Carpenter & Coen (2003) Science 299:1404-1407; Palatnik et al. (2003) Nature 425:257-263; Efroni et al. (2008) Plant Cell 20:2293-2306; Sharon et al. (2002) Nature 419:579-580" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L805-L1012>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_067_ripping_leaf_edge_waves.lean#L133-L174> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def marginal_growth_increment (gamma0 m_rem a_boost : Nat) : Nat :=
  gamma0 * m_rem * a_boost
theorem tcp_arrested_marginal_growth_increment (gamma0 a_boost G : Nat) :
    marginal_growth_increment gamma0 0 a_boost = 0 ∧
    (∀ m1 m2 : Nat, m1 ≤ m2 →
      marginal_growth_increment gamma0 m1 a_boost ≤ marginal_growth_increment gamma0 m2 a_boost) ∧
    (∀ m_rem R b : Nat,
      marginal_growth_increment gamma0 m_rem R ≤ marginal_growth_increment gamma0 m_rem (R + b)) ∧
    (∀ m_rem : Nat, G ≤ G + marginal_growth_increment gamma0 m_rem a_boost)
def excess_metric_numerator (g_mar g_int : Nat) : Int :=
  ((1 + g_mar) * (1 + g_mar) : Nat) - ((1 + g_int) * (1 + g_int) : Nat)
theorem developmental_excess_metric_nonneg (g_mar g_int : Nat) (h : g_int ≤ g_mar) :
    0 ≤ excess_metric_numerator g_mar g_int ∧ excess_metric_numerator g_int g_int = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dΓ_int/dt = γ_0 (1 - m),  dΓ_mar/dt = γ_0 (1 - m)(1 + β a/a_ref),  m(y,t) = σ((v_tcp t - (L - y))/w),  g_0(y,t) = ((1+Γ_mar)/(1+Γ_int))^2 - 1 ≥ 0,  m = 1 ⇒ dΓ = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/419579a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature01958>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng1835>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0911954106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1015162108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.91.086105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.044792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.045617>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.107.057521>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1079354>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1511/2004.3.254> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Non-Euclidean Föppl–von Kármán Thin-Sheet Elasticity, Negative Gaussian Curvature (K < 0) & Self-Similar Multi-Generation Edge Buckling Cascades" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.marginal_growth_increment" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.tcp_arrested_marginal_growth_increment" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "PIN1 Up-the-Gradient Pairwise Auxin Transport Mass Conservation (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that the PIN1 up-the-gradient exchange used to generate auxin convergence maxima (serration tips) is antisymmetric and conserves the two-cell auxin total, hence total lattice auxin changes only through production, decay and growth dilution | Variables: a_i: auxin in cell i; p_i: CUC2-gated PIN1 level; T: transport rate; κ: up-the-gradient polarisation strength; J_{i→j}: PIN1-mediated efflux from i to j" ;
    dct:source "Smith et al. (2006) PNAS 103:1301-1306; Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103:1633-1638; Bilsborough et al. (2011) PNAS 108:3424-3429" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L776-L797>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_067_ripping_leaf_edge_waves.lean#L184-L195> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pin_pairwise_net_flux (f_ij f_ji : Int) : Int :=
  f_ij - f_ji
theorem pin_pairwise_transport_mass_conservation (a_i a_j f_ij f_ji : Int) :
    pin_pairwise_net_flux f_ij f_ji + pin_pairwise_net_flux f_ji f_ij = 0 ∧
    (a_i - pin_pairwise_net_flux f_ij f_ji) + (a_j + pin_pairwise_net_flux f_ij f_ji) = a_i + a_j ∧
    pin_pairwise_net_flux f_ij f_ij = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "J_{i→j} = T p_i a_i exp(κ a_j) / Σ_k exp(κ a_k),  p_i = p_max c_i/(c_half + c_i),  net_{ij} = J_{i→j} - J_{j→i} = -net_{ji},  Σ_i da_i|_transport = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/419579a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature01958>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng1835>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0911954106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1015162108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.91.086105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.044792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.106.045617>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.107.057521>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1079354>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1511/2004.3.254> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Non-Euclidean Föppl–von Kármán Thin-Sheet Elasticity, Negative Gaussian Curvature (K < 0) & Self-Similar Multi-Generation Edge Buckling Cascades" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.pin_pairwise_net_flux" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_067.pin_pairwise_transport_mass_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

